    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The only test class, `AcceptanceTest`, has 2 tests, both passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a derived `membershipTier` response field: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nSince this is a read-only value computed from the owner's own stored state, I followed the existing precedent for derived fields like `initials` (a computed getter on the model that MapStruct auto-maps) rather than the `Assign*` pipeline-step pattern used for *persisted* fields like `namesakeCount`/`membershipNumber`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a small computed `getMembershipTier()` getter (getter-only, never persisted), encapsulating just the tier rule. Null-safe on both `namesakeCount` and `email`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `membershipTier` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically. No mapper, DTO, or pipeline changes were needed.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`SILVER` when unique with email, `BRONZE` when no email) pass, and the full build is green.",
